{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_jwdz6klnpneedbalc6tehnq2co47655737bocl7dv2fq6faedfhq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All tests pass. Both `test_parsing_some_args` and `test_help_arg` pass successfully.\n\nSummary of what I implemented:\n\n**`src/snprintf.rs`** — Pure-Rust simplified port of the printf-family functions from `snprintf.c`. Since the function signatures take `&[&str]` rather than C varargs, conversions are treated as string substitutions with width/precision/zero-pad support — sufficient for the error formatting used by xopt.\n\n**`src/xopt.rs`** — Full port of the xopt parsing engine from `xopt.c`:\n- `xopt_context`: Builds a context wrapping the option list and flags.\n- `xopt_parse`: Iterates argv, dispatching each entry to `parse_arg` and collecting non-option arguments into the `extras` Vec, honoring `XOPT_CTX_KEEPFIRST` and `XOPT_CTX_POSIXMEHARDER`.\n- `parse_arg`: Distinguishes short (`-x`), long (`--foo`), `--`-doubledash, and extras, supporting condensed shorts, sloppy shorts, `--name=value`, and strict-mode error reporting that mirrors the C messages.\n- `xopt_get_arg` / `xopt_set` / `default_callback`: Look up options, dispatch the user callback or the default, and write into the data struct via raw pointer offsets (matching the C `offsetof` semantics required by the test). Numeric parsing supports `0x`/`0` prefixes like `strtol(..., 0)`.\n- `xopt_autohelp`: Computes column widths and renders the help text faithfully.\n- `XOPT_SIMPLE_PARSE!` macro: A safe, idiomatic Rust replacement for the C macro.\n\n`cargo build` succeeds and `cargo test` passes both test cases."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1289,"cache_read_input_tokens":82897,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1289,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d55ff28a-c83f-4875-8394-ed911f146815","uuid":"aa506825-f302-4793-af3c-9a5eb046a329"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":191926,"duration_api_ms":189692,"ttft_ms":2810,"num_turns":17,"result":"All tests pass. Both `test_parsing_some_args` and `test_help_arg` pass successfully.\n\nSummary of what I implemented:\n\n**`src/snprintf.rs`** — Pure-Rust simplified port of the printf-family functions from `snprintf.c`. Since the function signatures take `&[&str]` rather than C varargs, conversions are treated as string substitutions with width/precision/zero-pad support — sufficient for the error formatting used by xopt.\n\n**`src/xopt.rs`** — Full port of the xopt parsing engine from `xopt.c`:\n- `xopt_context`: Builds a context wrapping the option list and flags.\n- `xopt_parse`: Iterates argv, dispatching each entry to `parse_arg` and collecting non-option arguments into the `extras` Vec, honoring `XOPT_CTX_KEEPFIRST` and `XOPT_CTX_POSIXMEHARDER`.\n- `parse_arg`: Distinguishes short (`-x`), long (`--foo`), `--`-doubledash, and extras, supporting condensed shorts, sloppy shorts, `--name=value`, and strict-mode error reporting that mirrors the C messages.\n- `xopt_get_arg` / `xopt_set` / `default_callback`: Look up options, dispatch the user callback or the default, and write into the data struct via raw pointer offsets (matching the C `offsetof` semantics required by the test). Numeric parsing supports `0x`/`0` prefixes like `strtol(..., 0)`.\n- `xopt_autohelp`: Computes column widths and renders the help text faithfully.\n- `XOPT_SIMPLE_PARSE!` macro: A safe, idiomatic Rust replacement for the C macro.\n\n`cargo build` succeeds and `cargo test` passes both test cases.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"d55ff28a-c83f-4875-8394-ed911f146815","total_cost_usd":1.2183612499999998,"usage":{"input_tokens":21,"cache_creation_input_tokens":71041,"cache_read_input_tokens":584150,"output_tokens":19287,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creat